---
/**
 * pages/[...slug].astro
 *
 * Catch-all route for CMS-authored public pages. Three published sources claim slugs: `pages`/`posts`
 * content types (posts under `/posts/`) and the compositor's `design_page` type. `route-authority.ts`
 * merges them, fails the build on any duplicate slug (one owner per path), and resolves each entry to
 * the design template it renders *through*, if it names one (D4). No template named → renders exactly
 * as it did before the compositor existed (D3) — designs are strictly opt-in.
 *
 * Prerendered: `getStaticPaths()` enumerates both sources at build time over EmDash's HTTP API (a
 * Cloudflare Access service token). Only published slugs are built, so an unknown path matches no
 * route and gets the static 404 from the Cloudflare ASSETS binding — no D1/KV lookup. Publishing or
 * editing a page requires a rebuild to regenerate these static pages.
 *
 * Design pages ship ZERO JavaScript: Puck's `Render` (`@puckeditor/core/rsc`), no client directive, so
 * it server-renders to plain HTML. Theme tokens inject into the head as `--dtk-*` properties alongside
 * the component stylesheet. A design page does NOT auto-emit `<h1>{title}</h1>` — headings come from
 * the canvas — while a Portable-Text page still does, preserving pre-compositor output.
 *
 * As a rest-parameter route this has the lowest routing priority — explicit files (index.astro,
 * privacy-policy.astro, /admin, /api) always win.
